 \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Library reserve material detail bridge table linking reserve catalog items, library subject offerings, course instructors, and material status per term. Used to count reserved materials per subject and to filter by library material status (e.g. 'U').\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Independent Activities Period (IAP) subject detail table: one row per IAP activity offered in a January term, with activity title/description, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, fee, prerequisites, preregistration deadline, cancellation and multiple-session flags, and foreign keys to category, sponsor, session, and person tables.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"TIP material dimension table describing textbook materials: title, author, edition, publisher, year, ISBN, new/used shelf prices and rental prices, and information source. Referenced by TIP_DETAIL via TIP_MATERIAL_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"TIP_MATERIAL\", \"name\": \"TIP_MATERIAL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"TIP material status lookup table decoding material status keys/codes used in TIP_DETAIL. Holds 12 status rows where key and code are identical: 'RQ' = Required, 'EO' = Electronic options, 'RC' = Recommended, 'PC' = Val-u option, 'BR' = Bookstore recommends, 'CL' = Go to class first, 'NM' = Course has no materials, 'U' = Unknown, and four keys ('NL', 'NS', 'NB', and a blank/space key) that share a NULL description.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\", \"name\": \"TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"TIP_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"name\": \"TIP_DETAIL\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"concept\", \"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"name\": \"Course Material and Library Reserve Domain\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"name\": \"Term Code\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"name\": \"Subject Identifier\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"