      "content": "The database connection consistently returns \"Access denied\" (verified across multiple attempts), so I'll finalize based on the semantic-network evidence and precedent SQL, which is rich and unambiguous for this question shape.\n\n# Investigation Report\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (investigated in depth):**\n- **TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — one row per subject per term in the Textbook Information Program scope. Key columns: `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (offering department name), `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (joins SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE), `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (enrollment headcount), `IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL` ('Y'/'N' flag), `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` (PK, parent of TIP_DETAIL).\n- **TIP_DETAIL** — bridge table linking subjects offered to their course textbook materials: `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY` (FK to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED), `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, …, **'NM' = Course has no materials**), `SUBJECT_ID`, `TERM_CODE`, `ISBN`, `RECORD_COUNT`. Granularity: one row per subject-material-status combination per term.\n- **TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS** — lookup decoding TIP statuses; confirms 'NM' = \"Course has no materials\".\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT / STUDENT_DEPARTMENT** — department dimensions (code, name, full name, school). Used in precedents when department attributes (full name, degree-granting) are needed; not needed here since the question asks only for the department name.\n- **SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — alternative enrollment carriers (official registrar enrollment or library-scope snapshots); no course-material association of their own.\n\n**Column concepts:**\n- **column_concept_enrollment_measures** — decision guide: \"Questions about enrollment of subjects within the textbook program … Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS.\"\n- **column_concept_material_status_key** — TIP statuses are decoded by TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS; 'NM' means the course has no materials.\n- **column_concept_department_name** — for textbook-program analysis, \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of … TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\"\n\n**Concept:** **concept_course_material_programs** — decision guide: \"Questions about required/optional textbooks, ISBNs, or **whether subjects have course materials**: Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED … with TIP_DETAIL (TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY).\"\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Graph edges confirm: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED →(joins)→ TIP_DETAIL via `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY`; TIP_DETAIL →(joins)→ TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS via `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY`; TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED →(joins)→ SIS_DEPARTMENT/STUDENT_DEPARTMENT via `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`.\n- 54 metrics depend on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (retrieved via metrics_by_table), confirming it is the standard fact table for course-material + enrollment questions.\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences & Task Fitness\n\n| Requirement | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED + TIP_DETAIL | SUBJECT_SUMMARY | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| \"number of enrolled students\" | SUPPORTED (`NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, decision guide cites it for textbook-program scope) | SUPPORTED but official-registrar semantics (`SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER`) | SUPPORTED but library-reserve scope only |\n| \"at least one associated course material\" | SUPPORTED — TIP_DETAIL is the association table; exclude 'NM' per status lookup and session convention | NOT-SUPPORTED — no material link | Partial (library reserve only, different program) |\n| \"department name\" | SUPPORTED (`OFFER_DEPT_NAME`, per column_concept decision guide) | SUPPORTED (`DEPARTMENT_NAME`) | SUPPORTED (`OFFER_DEPT_NAME`) |\n| Grand total (null, total avg, total stddev) | SUPPORTED via `GROUP BY … WITH ROLLUP` (precedent dw_1288 uses WITH ROLLUP for exactly this \"(name, null, total variance and stddev)\" shape) | same | same |\n\n**Wording anchoring:** \"at least one **associated** course material\" lexically matches the TIP_DETAIL association rows; per the documented status domain, 'NM' = \"Course has no materials\", so a course has at least one material iff it has a TIP_DETAIL row with status ≠ 'NM' (session tip confirms: \"'at least one teaching material' should exclude 'NM'\").\n\n**Precedent usage evidence:**\n- AVG/STDDEV of `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` grouped by department: dw_1221 (avg+stddev with a material-status filter via join to a material-detail table), dw_1689, dw_4640, dw_4527, dw_3356 — 5+ precedents.\n- \"has course materials\" filter precedents: dw_1689/dw_1954/dw_2181 use `IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL='N'`; dw_1221/dw_3493/dw_4756 use material-detail joins with status filters. The \"at least one associated … material\" wording + NM-exclusion convention anchors to the TIP_DETAIL join with `<> 'NM'`.\n- WITH ROLLUP grand-total precedent: dw_1288.\n\n## 4. Business Usage\nTIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the textbook-program fact table used for per-department enrollment statistics; TIP_DETAIL determines material association/status; together they answer \"which subjects have course materials and what is their enrollment\" — exactly this task's pattern.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n- semantic_search (4 calls, all-type + targeted table/metric/column_concept) ✔\n- semantic_get: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_DETAIL, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SIS_DEPARTMENT, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS, 4 column_concepts, concept_course_material_programs, metrics dw_1689/dw_1954/dw_1288/dw_1350/dw_4640/dw_2958/dw_3493/dw_4756/dw_4527/dw_1221/dw_2181/dw_3356 ✔\n- semantic_graph: metrics_by_table(TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED), query_neighbors(TIP_DETAIL) ✔\n- mysql_query: attempted 3× — **database returns \"Access denied\" (1045)**; data verification impossible; SQL grounded in documented schema/precedents instead.\n- Remaining Phase-1 entities (facilities/space/Moira/CIP/IAP tables etc.) were screened as unrelated to departments×enrollment×course-materials and discarded per Phase-1 relevance rules.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n**6a.** Use `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` (measure `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, group key `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`) joined to `TIP_DETAIL` on the documented FK `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY`, filtering `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY <> 'NM'` (\"at least one associated course material\").\n\n**6b.** Single-level aggregation `GROUP BY OFFER_DEPT_NAME WITH ROLLUP` — the ROLLUP super-aggregate row is exactly `(NULL, total average, total stddev)` computed over all departments' rows, matching the requested grand-total format (dw_1288 precedent). Bare `STDDEV()` per the tip; no rounding.\n\n**6c.** Data: TIP_DETAIL is the only association table between offerings and course materials; FK join documented in both tables' column definitions. Semantic-network: enrollment decision guide routes textbook-program enrollment questions to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS; department-name guide routes to OFFER_DEPT_NAME; material-status guide + 'NM' semantics support the exclusion filter. Business: 5+ metric precedents compute per-department AVG/STDDEV of this exact column, and dw_1288 establishes the WITH ROLLUP grand-total convention.\n\n**6d.** Alternative: `IS_NO_COURSE_MATERIAL='N'` flag (dw_1689-style) avoids material-row fan-out, but the question's \"at least one **associated** course material\" wording plus the NM-exclusion convention anchor to the TIP_DETAIL join, consistent with dw_1221's join-based avg/stddev precedent.\n\n",
