  "content": "The final SQL has been submitted. \n\n**Summary of the solution:**\n\n```sql\nSELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME,\n       AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrolled_students,\n       STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS stddev_enrolled_students\nFROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso\nJOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY = td.TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY\nWHERE td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY <> 'NM'\nGROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME WITH ROLLUP\n```\n\n**Key decisions and their evidence:**\n1. **Table choice**: `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED` joined to `TIP_DETAIL` — the enrollment decision guide explicitly routes \"enrollment of subjects within the textbook program\" questions to `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, and the course-material concept guide says \"whether subjects have course materials\" questions use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED with TIP_DETAIL.\n2. **\"At least one associated course material\"**: implemented as the FK join to `TIP_DETAIL` (the association table) with `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY <> 'NM'`, since the TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS lookup documents 'NM' = \"Course has no materials\" — matching the session convention that \"at least one teaching material\" excludes 'NM'.\n3. **Department name**: `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` per the department-name column concept's decision guide for textbook-program analysis.\n4. **Grand total row**: `GROUP BY ... WITH ROLLUP` produces exactly the requested `(NULL, total average, total stddev)` super-aggregate row over all departments — the same convention used by precedent metric dw_1288.\n5. **STDDEV**: bare `STDDEV()` (never STDDEV_POP), no rounding anywhere, per the question's explicit instruction.\n\nNote: live data verification via `mysql_query` was not possible (the database consistently returned \"Access denied\" error 1045 across three attempts), so the query was grounded entirely in the documented schema, join relationships from the semantic graph, and established precedent metric SQL.",
